      "status": "archived",
      "title": "All about that proxy.",
      "summary": "Today we are joined by ⁠Dr. Renée Burton⁠, VP of Threat Intelligence at ⁠Infoblox⁠, discussing their work on Lurking Lizard, \"Fake Installers, Fake Reviews, Fake Services – Real Proxies, Real.\" The research uncovers Lurking Lizard, a threat actor that has operated since at least 2022 by using fake software installers, VPNs, and lookalike domains to secretly turn victims’ devices into residential proxy nodes. Researchers identified more than 230 related domains and connected seemingly separate campaigns—including fake 7-Zip, downloader tools, and WireVPN—through shared infrastructure, tracking…",
